The Girl Next Door is a 2004 American romantic sex comedy film directed by Luke Greenfield and written by David Wagner, Brent Goldberg, and
Stuart Blumberg, and starring Emile Hirsch, Elisha Cuthbert, Timothy Olyphant, James Remar, Chris Marquette, and Paul Dano.

13
01:02:10,434 --> 01:02:16,434
The story follows Matthew Kidman, a high school senior who falls in love with his new
neighbor, Danielle, and discovers she is a former adult film actress.

14
01:06:57,391 --> 01:07:03,391
Development for The Girl Next Door began as early as 2001.

15
01:11:44,347 --> 01:11:50,347
The film's screenplay was partly inspired by Risky Business (1983).

16
01:16:31,304 --> 01:16:37,304
Principal photography occurred primarily in Los
Angeles County, California and Las Vegas.

17
01:21:18,260 --> 01:21:24,260
The film features cinematography by Eric Alan
Edwards and a score by Paul Haslinger.

18
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
The Girl Next Door premiered at the Texas Film Festival on February 18, 2004, before being
theatrically distributed nationwide by 20th Century Fox on April 9, 2004.

19
